# Changes to the CI that judges PRs need the owner's review, so a PR can't
# rewrite its own checks (lead-verified gate, 2026-10-23). The main ruleset requires
# code-owner review (require_code_owner_review, checked 2026-10-29), so this is enforced.
# It does not dismiss stale approvals on push.
/.github/CODEOWNERS   @sethdford
/.github/workflows/   @sethdford
/scripts/ci/          @sethdford

# Quality gates. They fail only on what a PR adds, measured against its merge base
# (merge-base.ts below); these files decide what counts as a violation, so a change to
# one changes the rule for every PR.
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/architecture-layers.ts @sethdford
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/merge-base.ts @sethdford
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/decisions.ts @sethdford
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/architecture-baseline.generated.json @sethdford
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/kernel-duplicates-baseline.json @sethdford
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/ratchet-baseline.json @sethdford
/knip.json @sethdford
# The gate code itself, the flag tooling and the flag lifecycle rules (code-owner review
# required, as above).
/apps/cli/src/commands/quality/ @sethdford
/scripts/flags/ @sethdford
/src/config/flag-lifecycle* @sethdford

# Autonomy lanes (scripts/ci/autonomy-policy.json; the "Autonomy Lanes" check). Crisis:
